entionally kept separate?","This field is actually not used - I\u0027ll remove it in the next PR"],"path":"x-pack/plugin/migrate/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/system_indices/action/AbstractFeatureMigrationIntegTest.java","id":36906,"created_at":"2025-02-28T19:02:57Z","original_position":53,"side":"RIGHT","position":53,"submitted_on_commit":"1c1cc6f59076424f55f9748c6afb3bfcc0bd4d53","diff_hunk":"@@ -77,10 +78,11 @@ public abstract class AbstractFeatureMigrationIntegTest extends ESIntegTestCase\n     static final int INDEX_DOC_COUNT \u003d 100; // arbitrarily chosen\n     static final int INTERNAL_MANAGED_FLAG_VALUE \u003d 1;\n     static final String FIELD_NAME \u003d \"some_field\";\n-    public static final Version NEEDS_UPGRADE_VERSION \u003d TransportGetFeatureUpgradeStatusAction.NO_UPGRADE_REQUIRED_VERSION.previousMajor();\n+    public static final Version NEEDS_UPGRADE_VERSION \u003d SystemIndices.NO_UPGRADE_REQUIRED_VERSION.previousMajor();\n     public static final IndexVersion NEEDS_UPGRADE_INDEX_VERSION \u003d IndexVersionUtils.getPreviousMajorVersion(\n-        TransportGetFeatureUpgradeStatusAction.NO_UPGRADE_REQUIRED_INDEX_VERSION\n+        SystemIndices.NO_UPGRADE_REQUIRED_INDEX_VERSION\n     );\n+    protected static final int UPGRADED_TO_VERSION \u003d SystemIndices.NO_UPGRADE_REQUIRED_VERSION.major + 1;","submitted_line":85},"generatedCommentsNodes":[]},{"groundTruth":{"original_line":83,"line":83,"comment_lines":["[][83]"],"review_comment":["Curious, why the setOnce here?","Good question. To be honest, I do not know, but it is used in plugins everywhere this way. I\u0027ll ask about this in our channel."],"path":"x-pack/plugin/migrate/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/migrate/MigratePlugin.java","id":36909,"created_at":"2025-02-28T20:10:04Z","original_position":49,"side":"RIGHT","position":49,"submitted_on_commit":"1c1cc6f59076424f55f9748c6afb3bfcc0bd4d53","diff_hunk":"@@ -61,14 +73,19 @@\n import java.util.List;\n import java.util.function.Predicate;\n import java.util.function.Supplier;\n+import java.util.stream.Stream;\n \n import static org.elasticsearch.xpack.core.ClientHelper.REINDEX_DATA_STREAM_ORIGIN;\n import static org.elasticsearch.xpack.migrate.action.ReindexDataStreamIndexTransportAction.REINDEX_MAX_REQUESTS_PER_SECOND_SETTING;\n import static org.elasticsearch.xpack.migrate.task.ReindexDataStreamPersistentTaskExecutor.MAX_CONCURRENT_INDICES_REINDEXED_PER_DATA_STREAM_SETTING;\n \n public class MigratePlugin extends Plugin implements ActionPlugin, PersistentTaskPlugin {\n+    private final SetOnce\u003cSystemIndices\u003e systemIndices \u003d new SetOnce\u003c\u003e();","submitted_line":83},"generatedCommentsNodes":[]},{"groundTruth":{"original_line":196,"start_side":"RIGHT","start_line":189,"line":196,"comment_lines":["[][189]","[][190]","[][191]","[][192]","[][193]","[][194]","[][195]","[185][196]"],"review_comment":["Can you help me understand when this codepath is executed?  I\u0027m a bit unsure of the context that motivates the changes in this function.  Why do we now differentiate if `indexMigrationInProgress`, and then update the mappings/settings/indexName differently for each branch of execution?","The other branch is executed when the request comes from an external system (e.g. Kibana), where we ignore settings/mappings/aliases/index name from the request, instead taking them from the index descriptor. Here, when the request is part of a system index migration, it includes settings and mappings specifically created by `SystemIndexMigrator` for that process, so we use them. (I doubt there\u0027s any difference in real world, but some tests rely on this behavior). Additionally, we don\u0027t create an alias in this case because it already exists, pointing to the current index, and SystemIndexMigrator will handle it later. Finally, regarding the index name – an index with `descriptor.getPrimaryIndex()` already exists, and we need to create a new index with the name `descriptor.getPrimaryIndex() + SystemIndices.UPGRADED_INDEX_SUFFIX` and this is the name from the request.","We didn\u0027t need this logic before, because we were bypassing it using MetadataCreateIndexService directly, but it is not available from plugins without introducing another transport message, which is probably too much for now","That\u0027s helpful context, much appreciated!  ","Will this will still work when _creating_ a new managed/unmanged system index?  Asking since the paths you described are:\r\na) migration happening for managed system index\r\nb) migration happening for externally managed system index\r\nWill a request for a brand new system index (or a move to a system index) hit the same logic?\r\n\r\nNo reason to to think it won\u0027t be (since tests are passing), but thought it best to check with you to be sure.","This branch is under the `if (indexMigrationInProgress)` check, so it shouldn’t be executed for a completely new index. The condition `boolean indexMigrationInProgress \u003d cause.equals(SystemIndices.MIGRATE_SYSTEM_INDEX_CAUSE) \u0026\u0026 request.index().endsWith(SystemIndices.UPGRADED_INDEX_SUFFIX)` ensures that the request is part of migration. The `cause` value, as I understand it, can\u0027t be set via REST API, and the only place in the codebase where it\u0027s set to `SystemIndices.MIGRATE_SYSTEM_INDEX_CAUSE` is in `SystemIndexMigrator`. Therefore, any request hitting this logic is coming from migration process and not from the creation of a new system index.\r\n\r\nMove of an existing index to a system index doesn\u0027t execute this code - it is just a metadata update of the index: `org.elasticsearch.cluster.metadata.SystemIndexMetadataUpgradeService`. System index mappings update also doesn\u0027t involve reindexing: `org.elasticsearch.indices.SystemIndexMappingUpdateService`","Thanks for the explanation!"],"path":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/action/admin/indices/create/TransportCreateIndexAction.java","id":36904,"created_at":"2025-02-28T18:02:24Z","original_position":36,"side":"RIGHT","position":36,"original_start_line":189,"submitted_on_commit":"1c1cc6f59076424f55f9748c6afb3bfcc0bd4d53","diff_hunk":"@@ -173,30 +173,54 @@ private CreateIndexClusterStateUpdateRequest buildUpdateRequest(\n             .waitForActiveShards(request.waitForActiveShards());\n     }\n \n-    private static CreateIndexClusterStateUpdateRequest buildSystemIndexUpdateRequest(\n+    private static CreateIndexClusterStateUpdateRequest buildManagedSystemIndexUpdateRequest(\n         CreateIndexRequest request,\n         String cause,\n         SystemIndexDescriptor descriptor\n     ) {\n-        final Settings settings \u003d Objects.requireNonNullElse(descriptor.getSettings(), Settings.EMPTY);\n+        boolean indexMigrationInProgress \u003d cause.equals(SystemIndices.MIGRATE_SYSTEM_INDEX_CAUSE)\n+            \u0026\u0026 request.index().endsWith(SystemIndices.UPGRADED_INDEX_SUFFIX);\n \n+        final Settings settings;\n+        final String mappings;\n         final Set\u003cAlias\u003e aliases;\n-        if (descriptor.getAliasName() \u003d\u003d null) {\n+        final String indexName;\n+\n+        // if we are migrating a system index to a new index, we use settings/mappings/index name from the request,\n+        // since it was created by SystemIndexMigrator\n+        if (indexMigrationInProgress) {\n+            settings \u003d request.settings();\n+            mappings \u003d request.mappings();\n+            indexName \u003d request.index();\n+            // we will update alias later on\n             aliases \u003d Set.of();","submitted_start_line":189,"submitted_line":196},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The change from `-reindexed-for-9` to `-reindexed-for-{UPGRADED_TO_VERSION}` makes the suffix dynamic and adaptable to future versions. Ensure that this change does not introduce any issues in existing systems that rely on the specific suffix format.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/mai